**Keydown** is the formatting language of [[radii-office|Radii Office]]. Instead of clicking buttons, you type short **tags** around your text, and the text turns into formatting: #G#glossy chips#, =B=gel orbs=B=, #Y#gel highlights##, **bold**, headings, lists and dozens of interactive "applets". Many of its looks come from the [[frutiger-aero|Frutiger Aero]] style.

## How it works

In Writeout and Bitbook, a tag turns into its formatting the moment you press **Space** after it, and pressing **Enter** at the end of a line formats every tag left on that line. In OpenDB, Phosphor and other apps, tags are drawn whenever the text is shown. Most tags wrap your text in an opening and a closing tag, such as `#R#` and `#`. Typing `\\` at the end of a formatted piece steps back out of it.

Keydown text is saved in `.kd` files (Writeout documents and OpenDB entries) and `.kn` files (Bitbook notes), and those apps can open each other's files.

## Lines

Start a line with one of these and a space:

* `# Heading` makes a big heading, `## Heading` a smaller one and `### Heading` a third level.
* `#### Heading` makes the extra large **mega header**.
* `* item` makes a bullet point, and `> text` a quote.

## Basics

* `**bold**` gives **bold**, and `*italic*` gives *italic*.
* Backticks around a word show it in a `code` font.
* `&&spark&&` gives &&spark&&.

## Gel highlights

The first three tools of the Annotator, as tags: `#R#text##` is a highlight strip, `#R#text#_` a gel underline and `#R#text#~` a gel strike. They come in 13 colors:


* `#R#` red: #R#highlight## #R#underline#_ #R#strike#~
* `#O#` orange: #O#highlight## #O#underline#_ #O#strike#~
* `#GL#` gold: #GL#highlight## #GL#underline#_ #GL#strike#~
* `#Y#` yellow: #Y#highlight## #Y#underline#_ #Y#strike#~
* `#L#` lime: #L#highlight## #L#underline#_ #L#strike#~
* `#G#` green: #G#highlight## #G#underline#_ #G#strike#~
* `#TU#` turquoise: #TU#highlight## #TU#underline#_ #TU#strike#~
* `#T#` teal: #T#highlight## #T#underline#_ #T#strike#~
* `#C#` cyan: #C#highlight## #C#underline#_ #C#strike#~
* `#B#` blue: #B#highlight## #B#underline#_ #B#strike#~
* `#PR#` purple: #PR#highlight## #PR#underline#_ #PR#strike#~
* `#PK#` pink: #PK#highlight## #PK#underline#_ #PK#strike#~
* `#SL#` slate: #SL#highlight## #SL#underline#_ #SL#strike#~

## Bubble chips

Glossy rounded chips, written `#color#text#`:

* `#C#text#` #C#cyan#
* `#O#text#` #O#orange#
* `#G#text#` #G#green#
* `#R#text#` #R#red#
* `#PR#text#` #PR#purple#
* `#PK#text#` #PK#pink#
* `#Y#text#` #Y#yellow#
* `#B#text#` #B#blue#
* `#L#text#` #L#lime#
* `#T#text#` #T#teal#
* `#GL#text#` #GL#gold#
* `#SL#text#` #SL#slate#
* `#W#text#` #W#white#
* `#BK#text#` #BK#black#
* `#FG#text#` #FG#fog#
* `#TU#text#` #TU#turquoise#

## Gel orbs

Round glossy orbs, written `=color=text=color=`:

* `=Y=text=Y=` =Y=yellow=Y=
* `=R=text=R=` =R=red=R=
* `=G=text=G=` =G=green=G=
* `=C=text=C=` =C=cyan=C=
* `=B=text=B=` =B=blue=B=
* `=V=text=V=` =V=violet=V=
* `=P=text=P=` =P=pink=P=
* `=O=text=O=` =O=orange=O=
* `=MG=text=MG=` =MG=magenta=MG=
* `=LM=text=LM=` =LM=lime=LM=
* `=AQ=text=AQ=` =AQ=aqua=AQ=
* `=SL=text=SL=` =SL=slate=SL=

## Prefix tags

Tag chips with an exclamation mark in front, written `!#color#text#`:

* `!#A#text#` !#A#aqua#
* `!#G#text#` !#G#green#
* `!#O#text#` !#O#orange#
* `!#R#text#` !#R#red#
* `!#PR#text#` !#PR#purple#
* `!#PK#text#` !#PK#pink#
* `!#Y#text#` !#Y#yellow#
* `!#SL#text#` !#SL#slate#

## Text effects

* `~G~text~G~` Gel green flash
* `~U~text~U~` Liquid underline
* `~B~text~B~` Glossy border badge
* `~S~text~S~` Cyber glow spark
* `~L~text~L~` Liquid text glow
* `~M~text~M~` Reflected text block
* `~E~text~E~` Embossed glass text
* `~W~text~W~` Kinetic wave text

The older line tags `~H1~`, `~H2~`, `~H3~`, `~MH~`, `~BQ~` and `~BUL~` still work, but the line shortcuts above are easier.

## Applets

Applets are small interactive widgets that you can click, like switches, dials and counters. Wrap a label in the tag:

* `~FN~label~FN~` Foldout tab
* `~TS~label~TS~` Aqua switch
* `~SM~label~SM~` Glass stamp
* `~TB~label~TB~` State button (green)
* `~VD~label~VD~` Volume dial
* `~BC~label~BC~` Battery cell
* `~CD~label~CD~` Calendar desk
* `~SR~label~SR~` Star rating
* `~CC~label~CC~` Counter badge
* `~LK~label~LK~` Security latch
* `~PR~label~PR~` Playback ribbon
* `~CR~label~CR~` CPU gauge
* `~SI~label~SI~` Stepper mesh
* `~ORB~label~ORB~` Hydro orb (blue)
* `~SLS~label~SLS~` Lock slider
* `~VM~label~VM~` Gadget clock
* `~MT~label~MT~` Metal trigger
* `~IC~label~IC~` Inset check
* `~NO~label~NO~` Neon node (cyan)
* `~LS~label~LS~` Latch toggle
* `~TIM~label~TIM~` Gadget system clock

